- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/curlnoise.html
- Summary (EN): Generates fractal curl noise built on Perlin noise and outputs a UV layer named noise, meant as a direction input for nodes such as Distort or Flow Block Begin. Uses image coordinates.
- Résumé (FR) : Produit un bruit de rotationnel fractal en coordonnées image, utilisable comme champ de direction.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref: reference layer setting output size and metadata", "pos: optional UV layer replacing pixel image coordinates as the noise source", "time: layer whose per-pixel value sets the time", "octaves: optional amount multiplying Max Octaves", "roughness: optional amount multiplying Roughness"]

- Key parameters: ["Amplitude: multiplies the noise before Center", "Center: offsets the output range", "Element Size: basic feature size in image coordinates; Element Scale per axis with Per-Component Controls", "Offset: shifts the pattern in image coordinates", "Tile Size: repeat period in image coordinates", "3D Noise group (Animate, Pulselength, Timescale, Timeoffset, Loop Length): time variation and seamless loop", "Fractal group (Max Octaves, Lacunarity, Roughness, Octave Offset): octave stacking"]

- Caveats: ["Without the fractal process the node is equivalent to wiring Perlin noise into the Slope Direction COP.", "Uses image coordinates; use Curl Noise 3D for world-space coordinates.", "With tileable behaviour, Element Size and Lacunarity are rounded or clamped."]

